# Somnium Volandi's style, as the code is written (docs/CODE_REWORK_PLAN.md 2.8): two-space indents, braces on the
# line, short things on one line, a trailing comment set off by three spaces, 140 columns. A guide for new code,
# applied to the lines a change touches (clang-format-diff), never to whole files: a wholesale reformat would bury the
# history, and the tool breaks two things the code keeps on one line (a one-line function holding an if/else, a chain
# of one-line catches), which stay as written.
BasedOnStyle: Google
AlwaysBreakTemplateDeclarations: No
ColumnLimit: 140
IndentWidth: 2
ContinuationIndentWidth: 4
TabWidth: 2
UseTab: Never
BreakBeforeBraces: Attach
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: AllIfsAndElse
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: true
AllowShortBlocksOnASingleLine: Always
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: All
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: true
AllowShortLambdasOnASingleLine: All
AllowAllArgumentsOnNextLine: true
AllowAllParametersOfDeclarationOnNextLine: true
BinPackArguments: true
BinPackParameters: true
AlignAfterOpenBracket: Align
AlignOperands: Align
AlignTrailingComments: false
SpacesBeforeTrailingComments: 3
PointerAlignment: Left
DerivePointerAlignment: false
ReflowComments: false
SortIncludes: false
IncludeBlocks: Preserve
AccessModifierOffset: -1
NamespaceIndentation: None
FixNamespaceComments: true
Cpp11BracedListStyle: true
SpaceAfterCStyleCast: false
SpaceBeforeParens: ControlStatements
Standard: c++17
